  "raw": {
    "pillar": "Climate & Environment",
    "headline": "Can we bring back an extinct antelope? This project is trying.",
    "challenge": "The bluebuck, a unique antelope with a blue-grey hide, went extinct around 200 years ago. Its disappearance left a gap in the ecosystem, and many have wondered if it could ever return.",
    "solution": "Colossal Biosciences, a Texas biotechnology company, is taking on this challenge with a project to revive the bluebuck. Their work could have far-reaching implications for conservation and biodiversity.",
    "resultHeading": "The bluebuck could roam the Cape again",
    "resultLine": "This groundbreaking project aims to restore lost species and ecosystems — read more at the link in bio.",
    "whyMatters": "Bringing back extinct species like the bluebuck could help restore ecosystems that have been disrupted by human activity. It also offers hope for other endangered species and the future of conservation efforts.",
    "engagementQuestion": "What do you think: should we bring back extinct species?",
    "captionLead": "Imagine seeing an extinct antelope roam the Cape again! Colossal Biosciences is on a mission to bring back the bluebuck, and their project could change the future of conservation. Read more about this incredible initiative at the link in bio.",
    "storyHashtag": "ConservationSuccess",
    "sources": [
